# ⛔ WITHOUT THESE, A CLEAN CHECKOUT RESOLVES AGAINST WHATEVER ~/.bazelrc SAYS.
#
# rules_walkthrough is published to registry.tbzl.dev, and tomato-bazel modules
# that consumers pair it with live only there. Pinning the registries here means
# this repo (and its CI, which has no personal ~/.bazelrc) resolves the same way
# on every machine instead of depending on developer config.
#
# ⚠ `--registry` ACCUMULATES rather than replaces, and FIRST MATCH WINS — so bcr
# must be listed explicitly and must come second, or every public module
# resolves from the tomato-bazel registry too.
common --registry=https://registry.tbzl.dev/
common --registry=https://bcr.bazel.build/

# Local overrides (not checked in).
try-import %workspace%/.bazelrc.user
